## Context

Phase 1 keeps the forge as the authority; the outbound bridge makes the
`.dyne` file the single source for the PR description. This closes part
of the recorded pain (the forge-parsing traps in the maintainer's
harness failure log): the PR body becomes generated output, never
hand-parsed truth.

## Scope

- a command that renders PR title and body from `tickets/merges/<branch>.dyne`:
  Title header as the PR title, the discussion's opening post as the
  body, `Closes:` values passed through as text
- offline invariant intact: dyne prints, carrying no network code; the
  caller pipes the output to the forge tooling of the day
- exact command shape (a `show` flag vs a dedicated verb) is decided in
  implementation and recorded here

## Historical exit criteria

These criteria are candidates only. Before work starts, revise them to match
the decision in 0271; if Dyne is not justified, do not implement them.

- [ ] PRs for dyne-carrying branches are opened with generated bodies
      (dogfooded on this repo)
- [ ] round-trip honesty: nothing in the PR body exists only on the
      forge

## Design reassessment (2026-11-04)

Git notes are the review-evidence store, as the author confirmed. The earlier
`tickets/reviews/` proposal is superseded. Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md`
for the current harness evidence and the remaining decision. The scope above
records the original design candidates; it does not authorize implementation.
Ticket 0271 must first establish a concrete unmet need and decide whether a
separate Dyne object is warranted. Subsequent format and implementation work
is conditional on that decision. This ticket remains open.
